{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>One who digs a pit.</b> Know that גומץ is singular, and there is no second [form], nor is there a [related] root in the Bible. And חופר indicates its meaning, which is like כרה בור (he dug a pit) and יחפרהו (it will be dug). It is possible that this matter turns back upon the ruler who does the opposite of truth, and breaches a fence that the ancients built. Or its meaning may be about the fool, and the sense is: even though there are found in the world things contrary to truth, they are few; but in the majority, one who digs a pit — into it he falls. And the sage who sees what is born will not fall."], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:28:53.764373214Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}